  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Scope: What a Name Means and Where",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Binding, Not Value",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scope = the region where a binding resolves",
            "Binding = a name paired with a value slot",
            "The binding is the pair, not the value in it",
            "Resolvable = reachable by that name, right here"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Scope Kinds",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Kind",
            "Made by",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Global",
              "script top level",
              "var g = 1"
            ],
            [
              "Function",
              "body + params",
              "function f(a)"
            ],
            [
              "Block",
              "{ } braces",
              "if / for / bare"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Lexical, Not Dynamic",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scope is fixed by where code is written",
            "So the engine resolves names before running",
            "Dynamic scope (bash, old Lisp) uses the caller frame",
            "JS never does; only `this` follows the call site"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Walking the Chain",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "inner block",
              "enclosing function",
              "module / script",
              "global",
              "ReferenceError"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "First match wins and the lookup stops there",
            "Chain exhausted, no match = ReferenceError",
            "undefined = binding found, holds no value yet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Shadowing",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "let x = 1;",
            "function f() {",
            "  let x = 2; console.log(x); // 2",
            "}",
            "f(); console.log(x); // 1"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inner name hides the outer for the whole inner scope",
            "Outer binding still exists, just unreachable by name"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Global Object Gotcha",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Top-level declaration",
            "On globalThis?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "var / function",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "let / const / class",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "anything in a module",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Scope: What a Name Means and Where (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Leaks and Strictness",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sloppy mode: `x = 1` on an undeclared name makes a global",
            "'use strict' turns that into a ReferenceError",
            "Module top-level `var` is module-scoped, never global"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Narrowest Scope That Works",
          "text": "Fewer names alive means fewer collisions and less to hold in your head."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Whole Comparison",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Row",
            "var",
            "let",
            "const"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Scope",
              "function",
              "block",
              "block"
            ],
            [
              "Hoists to",
              "undefined",
              "TDZ",
              "TDZ"
            ],
            [
              "Redeclare",
              "legal",
              "SyntaxError",
              "SyntaxError"
            ],
            [
              "Reassign",
              "yes",
              "yes",
              "TypeError"
            ],
            [
              "On globalThis",
              "yes",
              "no",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Redeclaring Is Parse-Time",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`var x; var x;` is legal and silent",
            "`let x; let x;` throws before any code runs",
            "`var x = 1; let x = 2;` is illegal in either order",
            "Parse error = nothing in the file executes at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. const Freezes the Binding",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const arr = [1, 2];",
            "arr.push(3);   // fine, the object is mutable",
            "arr = [];      // TypeError",
            "Object.freeze(arr); // shallow, freezes value"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Error text: Assignment to constant variable",
            "`const x;` is a SyntaxError, initializer required"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Block Leak Demo",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "if (true) { var a = 1; let b = 2; }",
            "console.log(a); // 1, var ignores blocks",
            "console.log(b); // ReferenceError"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Loop-Body Semantics",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`let i`: a fresh binding is created each iteration",
            "`var i`: one binding shared by the whole loop",
            "That single difference is the classic closure bug"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "var vs let vs const: The Table",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Parameters Are Bindings",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Params are function-scoped, initialized on call",
            "A `let` of a param name in the body = SyntaxError",
            "A `var` of that name is legal and reuses the slot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Style Default",
          "text": "`const` first, `let` only when you must rebind, `var` never in new code — read it, do not write it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Nothing Actually Moves",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Creation phase registers every declaration first",
            "They land in the scope's environment record",
            "Only then do statements execute, top to bottom",
            "'Code moves up' is a story, not the mechanism"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Two-Phase Model",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "var",
            "let / const",
            "function"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Creation",
              "undefined",
              "uninitialized",
              "fully ready"
            ],
            [
              "Execution",
              "assigned in place",
              "assigned at line",
              "already usable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Declarations Hoist Whole",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "greet();  // works, body already registered",
            "function greet() {",
            "  console.log('hi');",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. var Hoists the Name Only",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "console.log(x); // undefined, not an error",
            "var x = 5;      // assignment stays right here",
            "console.log(x); // 5"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Expressions Do Not",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "f();  // TypeError: f is not a function",
            "var f = function () {};",
            "g();  // ReferenceError, const is in TDZ",
            "const g = () => {};"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arrows behave exactly like function expressions",
            "`class C {}` hoists but sits in TDZ, like `let`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Hoisting: What Really Moves",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Precedence in One Scope",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Function declarations register before `var`s",
            "A same-name `var` does not overwrite the function",
            "It only wins once its assignment actually runs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Two Traps",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Block function declarations: strict-legal but block-scoped",
            "Never rely on them; use `let f = function () {}`",
            "Hoisting is per-scope: a fn's `var` is invisible outside"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why the Style Rule Exists",
          "text": "Declare at the top of the scope and hoisting stops being observable at all."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What the TDZ Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Starts where a let/const/class binding's scope starts",
            "Ends at the line that initializes the binding",
            "Touching the name inside that window throws"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Read the Error Exactly",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Message",
            "Diagnosis"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cannot access 'x'...",
              "declared, in TDZ"
            ],
            [
              "x is not defined",
              "never declared"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Temporal, Not Spatial",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "It depends on when execution passes the initializer",
            "A function written above but called after runs fine",
            "Line position by itself decides nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Three Demos",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ console.log(x); let x = 1; } // throws",
            "{ console.log(y); var y = 1; } // undefined",
            "let z = 1;",
            "{ console.log(z); let z = 2; } // throws too"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Last case: the inner `let` shadows from the block start",
            "So the outer `z` is unreachable, not a fallback"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. typeof Is Not a Guard",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "typeof nope; // 'undefined', safe",
            "typeof x;    // throws if a let x is below",
            "function f(a = b, b = 2) {}",
            "f();         // param default hits the TDZ"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Temporal Dead Zone",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Why It Exists",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use-before-define is a loud error, not silent undefined",
            "`const` can therefore never be observed as undefined",
            "Loop `let`: fresh binding per pass, copied forward",
            "Bundled 'Cannot access' usually means a circular import"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Closures Begin Here",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Closure = a function plus the environment it was made in",
            "It keeps that environment alive after the outer returns",
            "Every JS function is one; it matters when it outlives"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function counter() {",
            "  let c = 0;",
            "  return () => ++c;",
            "}",
            "const inc = counter(); inc(); inc(); // 2"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Capture Is by Binding",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "let v = 1;",
            "const show = () => v;",
            "v = 2;",
            "show(); // 2, not 1"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The inner function sees later mutations of the name",
            "Nothing is snapshotted at creation time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. One Call, One Environment",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each outer call creates a brand-new environment",
            "Two counters from counter() share no state",
            "Two functions from the same call share one env",
            "That sharing is what makes get/set pairs work"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Engine Mechanics",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The stack frame dies; the record moves to the heap",
            "A reachable closure holds a reference to that record",
            "The closure stores [[Environment]], an internal pointer",
            "That record chains outward to the global record"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. What Gets Captured",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "By spec: the whole environment record, not just names used",
            "Engines usually optimize away unreferenced slots",
            "Do not rely on it for large captured objects"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Closures: Bindings, Not Snapshots",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Closure vs Object",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Closure",
            "Object"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "State",
              "unreachable",
              "a property"
            ],
            [
              "Inspect",
              "impossible",
              "Object.keys"
            ],
            [
              "Access",
              "only via fn",
              "dot / bracket"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. The Loop Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {",
            "  setTimeout(() => console.log(i));",
            "}",
            "// 3, 3, 3"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`var i` is one function-scoped slot for all three",
            "Timers fire after the loop is over, and `i` is 3",
            "3 not 2: the loop exits on the increment that fails"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Not Late, Just Changed",
          "text": "The closure is never running behind — the shared variable simply moved on. Fix the binding, not the timing."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Fix 1 — let",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {",
            "  setTimeout(() => console.log(i));",
            "}",
            "// 0, 1, 2 — a fresh i each pass"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Fix 2 — IIFE Parameter",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {",
            "  (function (j) {",
            "    setTimeout(() => console.log(j));",
            "  })(i); // j is a new binding per call",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Fix 3 — Bind the Value",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// inside the same var loop:",
            "setTimeout(console.log.bind(null, i), 0);",
            "// i is read at bind time, frozen into the fn"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Loop Header Rules",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Header",
            "let",
            "const"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "for (;;)",
              "per-iteration",
              "SyntaxError"
            ],
            [
              "for...of",
              "per-iteration",
              "legal"
            ],
            [
              "for...in",
              "per-iteration",
              "legal"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Same Bug, Other Clothes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Handlers attached in a `var` loop all report the last index",
            "`fns.push(() => i)` with `var`: all three return 3",
            "An `await` inside a `var` loop aliases the same way",
            "Per-iteration `let` fixes every one of them"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Three Fixes, Then IIFEs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. The Non-Fix",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`setTimeout('console.log(' + i + ')')` works by accident",
            "String eval is slow, unsafe, and breaks minification"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. IIFE Forms",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "(function () { /* private */ })();",
            "(function () { /* ... */ }()); // Crockford",
            "(() => { /* arrow */ })();"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A statement starting with `function` parses as a declaration",
            "Declarations cannot be invoked; parens force expression",
            "`!function(){}()`, `+`, `void` coerce the same way",
            "Arrow IIFE has no own `this`/`arguments`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Async IIFE",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "(async () => {",
            "  await main();",
            "})(); // top-level await in CJS or a script"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why IIFEs Existed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pre-ES6, `var` was it and everything leaked to global",
            "An IIFE was the only private scope available",
            "Bundlers still emit an IIFE wrapper per bundle",
            "That keeps bundle internals off the page's globals"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Parameter Injection",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "(function ($, undefined) {",
            "  // $ is a local, minifies to one char",
            "  // undefined really is undefined in here",
            "})(jQuery);"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Run-Once Setup",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const config = (function () {",
            "  const raw = readFile();",
            "  return parse(raw); // only this survives",
            "})();"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The ASI Hazard",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A previous line with no semicolon plus `(` reads as a call",
            "Hence the defensive leading `;(function(){})()`",
            "Modern status: a bare block gives block privacy",
            "ES modules give file privacy; keep IIFEs for async top level"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "IIFE Uses, Module Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Module Pattern",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const store = (function () {",
            "  let items = []; // private, unreachable",
            "  const add = x => items.push(x);",
            "  return { add, count: () => items.length };",
            "})();"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An IIFE holds private state, returns public methods",
            "The methods close over it; nothing else can reach it",
            "Revealing variant: declare inner fns, return a name map",
            "One place to read the entire public surface"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Real Privacy",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Invisible to Object.keys and bracket access",
            "Skipped by JSON.stringify",
            "Not listed in a debugger's property inspector"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Singleton or Factory",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function makeStore() {",
            "  let items = [];",
            "  return { add: x => items.push(x) };",
            "} // one private environment per call"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The IIFE runs once, so you get exactly one instance",
            "Wrap it in a factory when you need many",
            "`class` with `#` fields: real privacy, shared prototype"
          ]
        },
        {
